&lt;p&gt;We’re a high-growth fintech company changing the retirement industry. We are backed by a number of investors. This includes funding from Marshall Wace and Baillie Gifford, as well as top investors such as &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2023/01/13/2588448/0/en/Human-Interest-and-BlackRock-Join-Efforts-to-Expand-Access-to-Retirement-Plans-for-Working-Americans.html#:~:text=Human%20Interest%20has%20secured%20approximately%20%24500%20million%20in%20funding%20to%20date&amp;amp;text=NEW%20YORK%20and%20SAN%20FRANCISCO,businesses%20across%20the%20United%20States.&quot;&gt;BlackRock&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2021/08/04/2274611/0/en/The-Rise-Fund-Leads-200M-Series-D-Investment-in-Human-Interest-to-Accelerate-Growth-and-Societal-Impact.html&quot;&gt;TPG (The Rise Fund)&lt;/a&gt;, SoftBank, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2021/02/11/2174214/0/en/Human-Interest-Completes-105M-Series-C-Following-Breakout-Year-in-2020.html&quot;&gt;Glynn Capital&lt;/a&gt;, NewView Capital, USVP, Wing, Uncork, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Corporate Counsel, you&#39;ll be the second corporate attorney on Human Interest&#39;s Legal team, reporting to the Assistant General Counsel, Corporate &amp;amp; Commercial. You&#39;ll own a broad slate of corporate, securities, and governance matters as Human Interest scales, and you&#39;ll also pitch in on commercial contracting, incident management, and regulatory matters. This is a new seat on a growing team, so the scope below reflects what you&#39;d be working on at the outset, but expect it to evolve along with the company and team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you get to do every day&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support corporate governance work for Human Interest Inc. and Human Interest Advisors as a primary function, including board and stockholder actions, subsidiary maintenance, and entity records&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and support board and committee materials; partner with the Finance team on board and committee preparation logistics, distribution, and tracking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the Legal portion of cap table and equity matters, including option grants, 409A coordination, executive compensation, and equity refresh cycles, partnering closely with the Finance and People teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support corporate finance and transactional activity across various transaction types, including equity, secondary transactions, debt, convertibles, and other sophisticated financing arrangements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain the governance and transactional playbooks, templates, and processes that allow Legal to scale with the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support IPO readiness activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage outside counsel on corporate and securities matters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead negotiation and execution of commercial agreements, including NDAs, vendor agreements, data processing agreements, and other contracts as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support M&amp;amp;A and other strategic transactions as they arise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring to the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You hold a J.D. from an ABA-accredited law school and are an active member in good standing of at least one U.S. state bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 4+ years of corporate and securities experience at a top-tier law firm, with at least one in-house role, preferably at a private, high-growth company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are experienced with a range of corporate transactions: equity, secondary transactions, debt, and other sophisticated financing arrangements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand cap table mechanics, equity administration, and corporate governance for multi-entity structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Public company reporting and securities compliance experience is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have owned and drafted and negotiated commercial contracts, including NDAs, vendor agreements, data processing agreements, and other transaction types&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve integrated AI tools into your legal work and understand how AI should shape contracting, transaction management, and legal operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in regulated industries (fintech, financial services, healthcare, or similar) is preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re pragmatic and business-minded — risk-aware, not risk-averse — and communicate clearly with both legal and non-legal stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re excited about this role but your background doesn&#39;t check every box above, we&#39;d still like to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll be the second Corporate hire on a rapidly growing legal team, with real room to shape how corporate and transactional work gets done&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll work directly with senior legal leadership and cross-functional partners across Finance, People, and the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll join a legal team that&#39;s already built real AI infrastructure — fluency rubrics, an AI-powered legal operating system, and day-to-day tooling — not just a company that talks about AI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broad, evolving scope across corporate, governance, and commercial work as Human Interest scales toward its next stage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why you will love working at Human Interest&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Human Interest is tackling one of our country&#39;s biggest challenges - closing the retirement gap. You&#39;ll be instrumental in architecting and scaling solutions that bring financial security to employees at small and medium-sized businesses nationwide. We’ve made significant progress, but there is still growth ahead, offering you a unique opportunity to solve complex problems, drive innovation, and advance your career alongside a dedicated, mission-driven team. We value hard work and recognize that our team&#39;s contributions are key to our continued success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join Human Interest and make a lasting impact by shaping the future of retirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our operating principles define how we work together as a team. They reflect Human Interest’s unique view on what’s important and what’s right. Documenting this core aspect of our culture helps employees make good decisions on their own. It also helps candidates considering career opportunities critically evaluate whether they will thrive at Human Interest.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer obsession&lt;/strong&gt;: We&#39;re all about creating amazing experiences for our customers. We put their needs first and go the extra mile to make them smile.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Long-Term Orientation&lt;/strong&gt;: We&#39;re not just playing for today; we&#39;re building a legacy. We think big, plan strategically, and invest in our future.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Autonomous and Accountable Teams&lt;/strong&gt;: We trust our team members to take ownership and make smart decisions. We empower you to be your best self!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An Escalating Bar for Talent and Performance&lt;/strong&gt;: We&#39;re constantly raising the bar and challenging ourselves to be better. We believe in growth and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fundamental Optimism&lt;/strong&gt;: We see the glass as half full (and then we fill it up with more amazing ideas!). We believe in the power of positivity and the potential for greatness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt; - At Human Interest, there are a number of factors that are used to determine the appropriate pay range for each position. We take into account the cost of labor for each position in various markets across the U.S. The base salary for this position spans $190,000 - $215,000&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;and represents the minimum in our lowest geographic region to a maximum&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;in our highest geographic region. The salary we offer to a new employee within this range is based on their location within the U.S., their relevant job-related skills, and experience. At Human Interest, base salary is one component of the overall total rewards package. Depending on the position, additional compensation components such as bonuses, commissions, and equity may be offered. All of our employees are offered a robust suite of physical, financial, and mental wellness benefits. In compliance with applicable laws, we do not inquire about salary history, or about criminal history prior to a conditional offer of employment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt; -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A great 401(k) plan: Our own! Our 401(k) includes a dollar-for-dollar employer match up to 4% of compensation (immediately vested) and $0 plan fees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Top-of-the-line health plans, as well as dental and vision insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive time off and parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Addition Wealth:&amp;nbsp; Unlimited access to digital tools, financial professionals, and a knowledge center to help you understand your equity and support your financial wellness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lyra: Enhanced Mental Health Support for Employees and dependents&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Carrot: Fertility healthcare and family forming benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Candidly:&amp;nbsp; Student loan resource to help you and your family plan, borrow, and repay student debt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly work-from-home stipend; quarterly lifestyle stipend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engaging team-building experiences, ranging from virtual social events to team offsites, promoting collaboration and camaraderie.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re a great place to work&lt;/strong&gt; (but don’t take our word for it)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here’s a list of our awards and accolades:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certified as a Great Place To Work® (2023-2025)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fortune Best Place to Work in the Bay Area (2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Best Places to Work by Built In (2023-2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;America’s Best Startup Employers by Forbes (2020-2022, 2024)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Top Company by Y Combinator (2020-2023)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inc. Fastest Growing Companies (2021)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
