&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://hi-contentful.imgix.net/4xN7JhmwCRuz3y9M8L8CF7/5c244c52cfc982bd1a348a80dc35d43b/hi-logo-new.svg?auto=format&amp;amp;ixlib=react-9.0.3&amp;amp;h=40&amp;amp;w=132&amp;amp;q=50&amp;amp;dpr=2&quot; alt=&quot;hi-logo&quot; width=&quot;132&quot; style=&quot;max-width: 100%;&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Human Interest is on a mission to ensure that people in all lines of work have access to retirement benefits.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;More than half of all working Americans are not saving enough for their future. Too often, it’s because they are employed by a company that doesn’t offer a retirement plan. Human Interest is changing that by making it affordable and accessible for small and medium-sized businesses to offer employees a path to financial independence through retirement savings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a high-growth fintech company changing the retirement industry. We are backed by a number of investors. This includes funding from Marshall Wace and Baillie Gifford, as well as top investors such as &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2023/01/13/2588448/0/en/Human-Interest-and-BlackRock-Join-Efforts-to-Expand-Access-to-Retirement-Plans-for-Working-Americans.html#:~:text=Human%20Interest%20has%20secured%20approximately%20%24500%20million%20in%20funding%20to%20date&amp;amp;text=NEW%20YORK%20and%20SAN%20FRANCISCO,businesses%20across%20the%20United%20States.&quot;&gt;BlackRock&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2021/08/04/2274611/0/en/The-Rise-Fund-Leads-200M-Series-D-Investment-in-Human-Interest-to-Accelerate-Growth-and-Societal-Impact.html&quot;&gt;TPG (The Rise Fund)&lt;/a&gt;, SoftBank, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2021/02/11/2174214/0/en/Human-Interest-Completes-105M-Series-C-Following-Breakout-Year-in-2020.html&quot;&gt;Glynn Capital&lt;/a&gt;, NewView Capital, USVP, Wing, Uncork, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Product management is changing. The best product managers no longer just write requirements and wait for engineering; they prototype their own ideas, pressure-test them with data, and use AI to move from problem to validated solution in days rather than quarters. We are looking for senior product managers who have internalized that shift and who want to apply it to one of the biggest unsolved problems in America: helping working people save for retirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own the product strategy for a meaningful surface area, lead a roadmap for a dedicated engineering team, and partner across Engineering, Design, Operations, Revenue, Customer Success, and Compliance to deliver accurate, timely, and transparent outcomes at scale. You will do this as an AI-augmented builder: using modern AI tooling both to sharpen how you work and to shape products that increasingly work on our customers’ behalf.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you get to do every day&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the vision and strategy for your product area end to end. Set a clear, opinionated direction, define the outcomes that matter, and rally your team and stakeholders behind a roadmap that delivers a great customer experience while achieving business goals and satisfying regulatory requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own the goals that measure success, quantify the business impact of what you ship, and rigorously track and report progress on a weekly and monthly basis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce artifacts that unblock engineering teams to deliver high-quality work on time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with other product teams so your solutions deliver a great end-to-end platform experience, not just a strong local one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dig into the data from first principles, form a point of view, and use it to validate assumptions and drive decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate tradeoffs and negotiate timelines with internal and external stakeholders, communicating with precision in both writing and conversation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you work with AI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We expect our senior product managers to use AI to work smarter and solve problems faster, and to bring good judgment about where AI belongs in the product itself.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prototype rapidly.&lt;/strong&gt; Use tools such as Figma Make, Claude Code, Codex, or similar to explore, validate, and demonstrate new ideas yourself, so you can align a team on direction with a working artifact rather than a document.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compress the busywork&lt;/strong&gt;. Apply AI to speed up research synthesis, requirements drafting, data exploration, and analysis so you spend your time on judgment, strategy, and customer understanding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build AI into the product.&lt;/strong&gt; Identify where copilots, agents, and intelligent automation genuinely improve the customer experience, and partner with engineering on what to build and how it should behave across success, failure, and edge cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring to the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 5+ years of product management experience, including owning a roadmap for a dedicated engineering team in a technical product area. Experience with financial or other regulated products is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated, hands-on use of AI tools to build and transform how you work, not just as a chatbot. You are comfortable vibe-coding front-end and UX changes yourself, and you can point to prototypes or interfaces where AI meaningfully changed the outcome or the pace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Builder mindset: &lt;/strong&gt;High agency and high urgency. You own problems end to end, turn zero-to-one ideas into real products, and do whatever it takes to execute complex projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical partnership:&lt;/strong&gt; You have partnered closely with engineers on complex systems at scale, can self-sufficiently root-cause issues, and can propose credible fixes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical rigor:&lt;/strong&gt; You are data-driven and think from first principles, and you are equally excited about 100 percent accuracy and 99 percent timeliness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business acumen:&lt;/strong&gt; You enjoy digging into how a business works, identifying how to make it better, and building product and technical solutions to do so.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Crisp, high-attention-to-detail written and verbal communication, with the ability to make complex technical concepts clear to any audience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education: &lt;/strong&gt;Degree in Computer Science, Business, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why you will love working at Human Interest&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Human Interest is tackling one of our country&#39;s biggest challenges - closing the retirement gap. You&#39;ll be instrumental in architecting and scaling solutions that bring financial security to employees at small and medium-sized businesses nationwide. We’ve made significant progress, but there is still growth ahead, offering you a unique opportunity to solve complex problems, drive innovation, and advance your career alongside a dedicated, mission-driven team. We value hard work and recognize that our team&#39;s contributions are key to our continued success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join Human Interest and make a lasting impact by shaping the future of retirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our operating principles define how we work together as a team. They reflect Human Interest’s unique view on what’s important and what’s right. Documenting this core aspect of our culture helps employees make good decisions on their own. It also helps candidates considering career opportunities critically evaluate whether they will thrive at Human Interest.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer obsession&lt;/strong&gt;: We&#39;re all about creating amazing experiences for our customers. We put their needs first and go the extra mile to make them smile.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Long-Term Orientation&lt;/strong&gt;: We&#39;re not just playing for today; we&#39;re building a legacy. We think big, plan strategically, and invest in our future.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Autonomous and Accountable Teams&lt;/strong&gt;: We trust our team members to take ownership and make smart decisions. We empower you to be your best self!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An Escalating Bar for Talent and Performance&lt;/strong&gt;: We&#39;re constantly raising the bar and challenging ourselves to be better. We believe in growth and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fundamental Optimism&lt;/strong&gt;: We see the glass as half full (and then we fill it up with more amazing ideas!). We believe in the power of positivity and the potential for greatness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt; - At Human Interest, there are a number of factors that are used to determine the appropriate pay range for each position. We take into account the cost of labor for each position in various markets across the U.S. The base salary for this position spans &lt;strong&gt;$171,000 - $207,000&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;and represents the minimum in our lowest geographic region to a maximum&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;in our highest geographic region. The salary we offer to a new employee within this range is based on their location within the U.S., their relevant job-related skills, and experience. At Human Interest, base salary is one component of the overall total rewards package. Depending on the position, additional compensation components such as bonuses, commissions, and equity may be offered. All of our employees are offered a robust suite of physical, financial, and mental wellness benefits. In compliance with applicable laws, we do not inquire about salary history, or about criminal history prior to a conditional offer of employment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt; -&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A great 401(k) plan: Our own! Our 401(k) includes a dollar-for-dollar employer match up to 4% of compensation (immediately vested) and $0 plan fees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Top-of-the-line health plans, as well as dental and vision insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive time off and parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Addition Wealth:&amp;nbsp; Unlimited access to digital tools, financial professionals, and a knowledge center to help you understand your equity and support your financial wellness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lyra: Enhanced Mental Health Support for Employees and dependents&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Carrot: Fertility healthcare and family forming benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Candidly:&amp;nbsp; Student loan resource to help you and your family plan, borrow, and repay student debt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly work-from-home stipend; quarterly lifestyle stipend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engaging team-building experiences, ranging from virtual social events to team offsites, promoting collaboration and camaraderie.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re a great place to work&lt;/strong&gt; (but don’t take our word for it)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here’s a list of our awards and accolades:&lt;/p&gt;
